{
  "version": 3,
  "format": "story",
  "title": "Why does my loop skip the last number?",
  "topic": "debugging/lldb-off-by-one",
  "genre": "trace",
  "style": "editorial-dark",
  "world": "debugger",
  "level": "beginner",
  "tags": [
    "debugging",
    "lldb",
    "breakpoint",
    "call-stack",
    "off-by-one",
    "assert"
  ],
  "cast": [
    {
      "id": "maya",
      "name": "Maya",
      "role": "Engineer chasing a failing test",
      "color": "#2F6F8F"
    }
  ],
  "glossary": [
    {
      "term": "breakpoint",
      "full": "A line where the debugger stops the program",
      "note": "Execution pauses before that line runs, and you can read every variable."
    },
    {
      "term": "call stack",
      "full": "The chain of functions that are running right now",
      "note": "Frame zero is the innermost call."
    },
    {
      "term": "off-by-one",
      "full": "A loop or index that stops one step early or late",
      "note": "i < n - 1 never reads the last element."
    }
  ],
  "key_points": [
    "Stop where the value goes wrong, then step: each step shows which line changed which variable.",
    "A breakpoint on the return line shows the final value without clicking through every pass.",
    "The call stack shows who called whom, so a failing assert points back to your own line."
  ],
  "sources": [
    "https://lldb.llvm.org/use/tutorial.html",
    "https://lldb.llvm.org/use/map.html",
    "https://man7.org/linux/man-pages/man3/assert.3.html"
  ],
  "beats": [
    {
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "The test wants fifteen. The function returns ten. Let's freeze it mid-loop.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "world.set",
          "world": "debugger",
          "file": "sum.c",
          "lang": "c",
          "code": [
            "#include <assert.h>",
            "#include <stdio.h>",
            "",
            "int sum_array(const int *a, int n) {",
            "    int total = 0;",
            "    for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++)",
            "        total += a[i];",
            "    return total;",
            "}",
            "",
            "int main(void) {",
            "    int a[5] = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5};",
            "    int s = sum_array(a, 5);",
            "    assert(s == 15);",
            "    printf(\"sum = %d\\n\", s);",
            "    return 0;",
            "}"
          ],
          "title": "lldb ./sum",
          "prompt": "(lldb)",
          "breakpoints": [
            5
          ],
          "line": 5,
          "reason": "breakpoint",
          "vars": {
            "a": "0x16fdfe370",
            "n": 5,
            "total": "1876944296"
          },
          "stack": [
            {
              "fn": "sum_array",
              "at": ":5"
            },
            "main",
            "start"
          ]
        },
        {
          "do": "dbg.cmd",
          "out": [
            "Process 99164 stopped",
            "frame #0: 0x00000001000004bc sum`sum_array(a=0x000000016fdfe370, n=5) at sum.c:5:9"
          ],
          "line_ms": 250
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "maya",
      "text": "We stopped on line five, the top of sum array. N is five, so five numbers get added.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "dbg.mark",
          "at": 0.55,
          "var": "n"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "maya",
      "text": "Total is garbage, because C never clears locals. Step over, and it becomes zero.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "dbg.mark",
          "var": "total",
          "at": 0.1
        },
        {
          "do": "dbg.step",
          "kind": "over",
          "at": 0.62,
          "line": 6,
          "vars": {
            "total": 0
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "Keep stepping. Each pass adds one number, and i climbs by one.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "dbg.mark",
          "off": true
        },
        {
          "do": "dbg.step",
          "kind": "over",
          "at": 0.2,
          "line": 7,
          "vars": {
            "i": 0
          }
        },
        {
          "do": "dbg.step",
          "kind": "over",
          "at": 0.5,
          "line": 6,
          "vars": {
            "total": 1
          }
        },
        {
          "do": "dbg.step",
          "kind": "over",
          "at": 0.8,
          "line": 7,
          "vars": {
            "i": 1
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "maya",
      "text": "Too slow. Put a breakpoint on the return, and continue.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "dbg.break",
          "at": 0.04,
          "line": 8,
          "cmd": "b sum.c:8",
          "out": [
            "Breakpoint 2: where = sum`sum_array + 92 at sum.c:8:12, address = 0x000000010000050c"
          ]
        },
        {
          "do": "dbg.continue",
          "at": 0.42,
          "cmd": "continue",
          "line": 8,
          "run_ms": 600,
          "pre": [
            "Process 99164 resuming"
          ],
          "out": [
            "Process 99164 stopped",
            "frame #0: 0x000000010000050c sum`sum_array(a=0x000000016fdfe370, n=5) at sum.c:8:12"
          ],
          "vars": {
            "total": {
              "value": 10,
              "tone": "bad"
            }
          },
          "drop": [
            "i"
          ],
          "stack": [
            {
              "fn": "sum_array",
              "at": ":8"
            },
            "main",
            "start"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "Ten, not fifteen. The loop quit one pass early.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "dbg.mark",
          "at": 0.7,
          "line": 6
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "maya",
      "text": "Add it up yourself: one plus two plus three plus four plus five is fifteen.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "dbg.cmd",
          "at": 0.0,
          "cmd": "p 1+2+3+4+5",
          "out": [
            "(int) 15"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "maya",
      "text": "The last element is five, and n minus one is only four.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "dbg.cmd",
          "at": 0.05,
          "cmd": "p a[4]",
          "out": [
            "(const int) 5"
          ]
        },
        {
          "do": "dbg.cmd",
          "at": 0.5,
          "cmd": "p n - 1",
          "out": [
            "(int) 4"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "Now let it run on, and the assert in main trips.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "dbg.mark",
          "off": true
        },
        {
          "do": "dbg.continue",
          "at": 0.15,
          "cmd": "continue",
          "line": 14,
          "reason": "assert",
          "run_ms": 700,
          "pre": [
            {
              "text": "Assertion failed: (s == 15), function main, file sum.c, line 14.",
              "tone": "err"
            },
            "Process 99164 resuming"
          ],
          "out": [
            "Process 99164 stopped",
            "* thread #1, queue = 'com.apple.main-thread', stop reason = hit program assert"
          ],
          "stack": [
            "__pthread_kill",
            "pthread_kill",
            "abort",
            "__assert_rtn",
            {
              "fn": "main",
              "at": "sum.c:14"
            },
            "start"
          ],
          "frame": 4,
          "vars_reset": true,
          "vars": {
            "a": "{1, 2, 3, 4, 5}",
            "s": {
              "value": 10,
              "tone": "bad"
            }
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "maya",
      "text": "Six frames. Libc is just aborting. Frame four is our line, and s is ten.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "dbg.mark",
          "at": 0.3,
          "frame": 4
        },
        {
          "do": "dbg.mark",
          "at": 0.62,
          "var": "s"
        },
        {
          "do": "define",
          "term": "call stack",
          "at": 0.2
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "There it is. I less than n minus one stops at three. An off by one.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "dbg.mark",
          "off": true
        },
        {
          "do": "dbg.mark",
          "at": 0.15,
          "line": 6
        },
        {
          "do": "define",
          "term": "off-by-one",
          "at": 0.4
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "maya",
      "text": "Kill it, drop the breakpoints, and fix the condition.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "dbg.exit",
          "at": 0.0,
          "cmd": "kill",
          "status": 9,
          "msg": "killed",
          "out": [
            "Process 99164 exited with status = 9 (0x00000009) killed"
          ]
        },
        {
          "do": "dbg.break",
          "at": 0.3,
          "lines": [
            5,
            8
          ],
          "off": true,
          "cmd": "breakpoint delete 1 2",
          "out": [
            "2 breakpoints deleted; 0 breakpoint locations disabled."
          ]
        },
        {
          "do": "dbg.mark",
          "off": true,
          "at": 0.62
        },
        {
          "do": "dbg.edit",
          "at": 0.66,
          "line": 6,
          "text": "    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "maya",
      "text": "Rebuild and run it again. Sum is fifteen, and the exit status is zero.",
      "visuals": [
        {
          "do": "dbg.cmd",
          "at": 0.0,
          "cmd": "platform shell cc -g -O0 -o sum sum.c",
          "cps": 40
        },
        {
          "do": "dbg.exit",
          "at": 0.45,
          "cmd": "run",
          "status": 0,
          "out": [
            "sum = 15",
            "Process 6579 launched: '~/demo/sum' (arm64)",
            "Process 6579 exited with status = 0 (0x00000000)"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "speaker": "narrator",
      "text": "Do not guess where a loop ends. Step to it and read the numbers.",
      "visuals": []
    }
  ]
}
